tiftung</publisher-name><fpage>11</fpage><lpage>31</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Streich</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reaktionen auf die Praxisgeb&#x000fc;hr &#x02013; was antworten die Betroffenen?</article-title><source>Gesundheitsmonitor Ein Newsletter der Bertelsmann Stiftung</source><year>2004</year><volume>2/04</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zok</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nach der Wirkung gefragt: Die Reform kommt an</article-title><source>Gesundheit und Gesellschaft</source><year>2004</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>38</fpage><lpage>41</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zok</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Das Arzt-Inanspruchnahmeverhalten nach Einf&#x000fc;hrung der Praxisgeb&#x000fc;hr. Ergebnisse aus zwei Repr&#x000e4;sentativumfragen unter 3.000 GKV-Versicherten</article-title><source>WIdO-monitor</source><year>2005</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>7</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Augurzky</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Bauer</surname><given-names>TK</given-names></name><name><surname>Schaffner</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Copayments in the German Health System: Does it work?</article-title><source>IZA Discussion Paper</source><year>2006</year><volume>2290</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>17</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Timm</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>K&#x000f6;rner</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Meyer</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Armut und Lebensbedingungen. Ergebnisse aus LEBEN IN EUROPA f&#x000fc;r Deutschland 2005</article-title><source>Statistisches Bundsamt, Wiesbaden</source><year>2006</year></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holst</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Kostenbeteiligung f&#x000fc;r Patienten &#x02013; Reformansatz ohne Evidenz! Theoretische Betrachtungen und empirische Befunde aus Industriel&#x000e4;ndern</article-title><source>Ver&#x000f6;ffentlichungsreihe der Forschungsgruppe Public Health, Schwerpunkt Arbeit, Sozialstruktur und Sozialstaat, Wissenschaftszentrum Berlin f&#x000fc;r Sozialforschung</source><year>2008</year></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Sociopolitical goals and perspectives of the Bertelsmann Stiftung     </article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.bertelsmann-stiftung.de/cps/rde/xbcr/SID-0A000F0A-AFC44F58/bst/xcms_bst_dms_16798_16799_2.pdf"/><comment>last access November 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>G&#x000fc;ther</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>B&#x000f6;cken J, Braun B, Schnee M, Amhof R</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Gesundheitsmonitor &#x02013; Stichprobe und Erhebungsmethode sowie Qualit&#x000e4;tsaspekte der Ergebnisse</article-title><source>Gesundheitsmonitor 2005 Gesundheitsversorgung und Gestaltungsoptionen aus der Perspektive von Bev&#x000f6;lkerung und &#x000c4;rzten</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>G&#x000fc;tersloh: Verlag Bertelsmann Stiftung</publisher-name><fpage>309</fpage><lpage>322</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Trojan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Nickel</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Amhof</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bocken</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>[Social factors influencing participation in self-help groups or organisations&#x02013;results from selected questions for the health monitor]</article-title><source>Gesundheitswesen</source><year>2006</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>364</fpage><lpage>375</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16826469</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1055/s-2006-926896</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>B&#x000f6;cken</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Braun</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Amhof</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Schnee</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><collab>Eds</collab></person-group><source>Gesundheitsmonitor 2006 Gesundheitsversorgung und Gestaltungsoptionen aus der Perspektive von Bev&#x000f6;lkerung und &#x000c4;rzten</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>G&#x000fc;tersloh: Verlag Bertelsmann Stiftung</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Helmert</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Strube</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>[The development of obesity in Germany in the period from 1985 until 2000]</article-title><source>Gesundheitswesen</source><year>2004</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>409</fpage><lpage>415</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15314732</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1055/s-2004-813324</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Helmert</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Buitkamp</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>[Changes in smoking habits in Germany between 1985 and 2002]</article-title><source>Gesundheitswesen</source><year>2004</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>102</fpage><lpage>106</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14994208</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1055/s-2004-813324</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Potthoff</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Heinemann</surname><given-names>LAJ</given-names></name><name><surname>G&#x000fc;ther</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A household panel as a tool for cost-effective health-related population surveys: validity of the "Healthcare Access Panel"</article-title><source>German Medical Science</source><year>2004</year><volume>2</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hair</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Tatham</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Black</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name></person-group><source>Multivariate Data Analysis</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>Upper Saddle River, NJ : Prentice Hall</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pauly</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Economics of Moral Hazard: Comment</article-title><source>American Economic Review</source><year>1968</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>531</fpage><lpage>537</lpage></citation